From 1c0546cae3dec682053827b3bbd2e0712bd46586 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: adrdsouza <102761952+adrdsouza@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 14:44:27 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] rightkit-media: pending Windows catalog rows and
 toolchain runtime notices

Merge the two proposed Windows rows into catalog/artifacts.json, both pending:
ffmpeg-7.1.5-export-ass-zimg-windows-x64 and ffprobe-7.1.5-windows-x64. The
proposal file is removed.

A static MinGW-w64 link carries the mingw-w64 C runtime, winpthreads and
libgcc (and libstdc++ when zimg and HarfBuzz are linked). Their notices are
added under third-party/, listed in the rows' noticeFiles, and copied into the
notices directory by the recipe from the toolchain's own licence files.

Build notes: zlib signature not checked, digest matched publisher.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
