From: adrdsouza <102761952+adrdsouza@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 14:53:31 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] rightkit-media: toolchain runtime components for static
 MinGW-w64 builds

TOOLCHAIN_RUNTIME_COMPONENTS names the runtime code a static MinGW-w64 link
carries into a Windows binary (mingw-w64-runtime, winpthreads, gcc-runtime).
Any variant may list them, decode included, each only under its own licence.

ALLOWED_COMPONENT_LICENSES gains LicenseRef-MinGW-w64-runtime and
GPL-3.0-or-later WITH GCC-exception-3.1; only those components may carry
them and every other GPL identifier is still refused. A component licence may
be a conjunction whose every term is allowed and named in the entry's
expression (MIT AND BSD-3-Clause for winpthreads).

The two pending Windows rows list the three components; the recipe records
the toolchain packages and their digests as evidence.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
